# L5R 5E - CELESTIAL REALMS: ADVENTURE SEEDS (FRAME)
# Source: Celestial Realms.

FRAME "L5R5e_CelestialRealms_AdventureSeeds" {
    NAME "Celestial Realms — Adventure Seeds"
    VERSION "0.4.1"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.4"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-09-02"
    DEPENDS_ON "L5R5e_Core_Core"

    DESCRIPTION "Adventure seeds presented in sidebars throughout Celestial Realms, for GMs to expand into full adventures."

    ENTRIES {
        ENTRY ^"SACRED TIMBER" {
            TYPE "hook"
            TAGS ["celestial-realms"]
            DESCRIPTION "Hook The PCs are discreetly contacted by Seppun Asahi, a member of the Seppun Astrologers, who protect the Emperor and his family from supernatural threats. Asahi asks the PCs to undertake an important but sensitive mission: securing a new source of wood for the statues of deceased Emperors that support the bridge at the Shrine to Hantei-no-Kami. The existing supply has been exhausted, and a new source will be needed after the death of the current Emperor. Asahi tells the PCs that a grove of ancient oaks in the mysterious Kitsune Mori is the best-known candidate, because the Kami Hantei once spent several days there speaking with Shinsei, the Little Teacher. Rising Action The PCs must visit the Fox Clan, a Minor Clan whose lands include the grove, and convince them to allow the trees to be harvested and the timber removed. He provides the PCs a letter proving they act on behalf of the Seppun, but he would prefer they not reveal the reason the wood is needed. The Fox daimyō, Kitsune Gohei, is curious, of course, but it will take some clever politics to convince him to allow the harvesting to go ahead. Explaining the need for the wood would almost certainly gain his cooperation, but can they get it without revealing what the wood will be used for? Climax The real problem, the PCs find, is that a powerful spirit inhabits the trees of the grove, and it, of course, resists any attempt to cut the trees. If the PCs battle the spirit and defeat it, they may render the grove spiritually impure and no longer suitable for the sacred statues. Can they convince, cajole, or even trick the spirit into allowing at least some of the trees to be cut?"
        }
    }
}
